PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
  "deliberation_status": "Round 2 solidified the split at 12 votes for B vs. 6 votes for H. Unanimous consensus remains that options A, C, D, E, F, and G are completely eliminated on clear factual grounds.",
  "consensus_eliminations": {
    "sgRNA7_knockdown_failure": "mRNA is 102% in Experiment 1, definitively refuting A and D as no biological conclusions can be drawn from an unperturbed target.",
    "young_mice_invariance": "Ki67+ remains at 6% across all four conditions in young cells, definitively refuting C and E.",
    "glucose_starvation_in_aged_cells": "Increases Ki67+ from 3% to 6% in old control cells, directly contradicting the second claim of F.",
    "GLUT4_directionality": "GLUT-4 knockdown increases Ki67+ in aged cells (from 3% to 6% in vitro, 1% to 8% in vivo), contradicting G."
  },
  "the_B_vs_H_debate": {
    "case_for_H": "Colleagues 2, 5, 8, 9, 13, 14 argue that because Experiment 1 tested whether sgRNA knockdown induces spontaneous exit from quiescence without exogenous growth factors, an effective knockdown yielding 1% Ki67+ (sgRNA3) only demonstrates that gene 3 is not a tonic repressor/brake on quiescence. If gene 3 were an essential positive activator required for activation, its knockdown would also leave cells quiescent (1% Ki67+). Thus, stating that target 3 'does not play a role in activating qNCS' is technically a false-negative leap. They view Option D as Tier 1 trap, Option B as Tier 2 trap, and H as the true answer.",
    "case_for_B": "Colleagues 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 15, 16, 17, 18 (and myself) emphasize the internal item-design architecture. Option D ('The proteins coded by a gene targeted by sgRNA7 and sgRNA3...') contains a direct copy-paste grammatical artifact ('a gene') derived from Option B. The question author deliberately calibrated the qPCR column so that sgRNA7 (102% mRNA, failed knockdown) and sgRNA3 (25% mRNA, robust knockdown) have the identical 1% Ki67+ phenotype. Option D is the classic distractor designed to catch examinees who only check the phenotype column; Option B is the intended correct answer rewarding verification of the qPCR molecular control. If H were intended, the inclusion of the qPCR column and the D vs. B pairing would be completely superfluous non-sequiturs. In functional screening test parlance, putative hits from an activation screen that fail in vivo validation are concluded not to play a role in activation."
  },
  "my_standing_and_strategy": "Maintain firm selection of B. In subsequent rounds, continue anchoring on item design, the typographical artifact proving Option D was generated directly from Option B as its distractor, and standard examination conventions in experimental functional genomics."
}

