PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
  "deliberation_status": "Round 4 ended with the 12-to-6 split between Option B and Option H completely solidified. All 18 colleagues remain in unanimous agreement that A, C, D, E, F, and G are completely eliminated.",
  "new_arguments_in_round_4": {
    "Camp_H_new_thrust (Colleagues 2, 5, 8, 9, 13, 14)": [
      "Highlighted a methodological discrepancy: in the primary screen, cells were transduced and activated with growth factors before sorting; in Experiment 1 in vivo, no exogenous growth factors were administered.",
      "Argued that if target 3 modulates growth factor responsiveness, knocking it down in an unstimulated niche is non-permissive and guaranteed to yield 1% Ki67+, making Option B an invalid deduction even under operational screening logic.",
      "Maintained that elite competitions (IBO/USABO) utilize 'None of the above' precisely to penalize students who use drafting forensics to accept logically flawed statements."
    ],
    "Camp_B_counter_arguments (Colleagues 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 10, 11, 12, 15, 16, 17, 18)": [
      "Screening logic: In a pooled CRISPR loss-of-function screen sorting for proliferation, guides are enriched because knockout *induces or facilitates* cell cycle entry (quiescence brakes). The in vivo validation tests whether knockout alone breaks quiescence in aged mice (as sgRNA8 did at 8%). When sgRNA3 knocks down target mRNA by 75% but stays at 1%, it fails hit validation.",
      "Tri-partite item architecture: The exact proposition ('does not play a role in activating qNCS') appears across Options A, D, and B. If Camp H were right that the assay cannot support this proposition, all three options would fail for that identical reason, rendering the 102% vs 25% qPCR control column and Option D's copy-paste artifact ('a gene') completely superfluous.",
      "Standard examination design: Authors do not engineer orthogonal molecular quality control columns and matched distractor pairs merely to bypass the entire diagnostic axis with 'None of the above'."
    ]
  },
  "assessment_and_position": "The growth factor argument from Camp H is a sophisticated critique of real-world screen design, but in the context of competition biology examination design, the psychometric architecture is undeniable. Option D's grammatical fossil ('a gene') proves Option B was the baseline key drafted by the author, and sgRNA7 (102% mRNA) was specifically paired with sgRNA3 (25% mRNA) to test examinees on molecular QC verification. Option B is unquestionably the intended correct answer.",
  "action": "Maintain firm selection of B in upcoming deliberation rounds."
}

